  "allocationUnit": "KES Millions",
  "notes": [
    "All figures are in KES millions based on the County Allocation of Revenue Act (CARA) equitable share schedule and Office of the Controller of Budget (OCOB) annual implementation reports.",
    "Equitable Share Allocation reflects the statutory formula developed by the Commission on Revenue Allocation (CRA) and approved by Parliament under Article 217 of the Constitution.",
    "Own-Source Revenue (OSR) includes locally collected property rates, single business permits, parking fees, market cess, hospital user fees, and park entry revenues (such as Maasai Mara in Narok County).",
    "Absorption rate = (actual total recurrent and development expenditure / total available revenue) × 100.",
    "Nairobi City County (#047), Nakuru (#032), Turkana (#023), Kakamega (#037), Kiambu (#022), and Kilifi (#003) receive the largest equitable share allocations due to population, land area, and poverty index weights.",
    "Data sourced from the Commission on Revenue Allocation (CRA), County Allocation of Revenue Act, and Office of the Controller of Budget (cob.go.ke)."
